d skills, although, yeah, that, so we, we, we, the idea here is these systems are, are like libraries of knowledge and we can kind of build on them and uh, create a system to help refine them and to become better essentially. And, and that's gonna be tricky to do to actually get good results. However, rather than have these things buried away in like a Claude skills folder where they're harder to see and just, I don't know, it feels like having a page for them would make a lot of sense. And so, you know, it is, it is like an AI system. However, it's also like a human system. It's just a system that, you know, whether we're using AI or whether, you know, a human were reading it and browsing it, It's sort of the same thing. It's just like, you know, all the code based, you know, like uh, code formatting, you know, all the um, all the opinionations, all the like recommendations, all the things to do or not to do when it comes to code. And so code is HTML, CSS, JavaScript, But you know, the, the framework slash code directory specifically is all about the code in the framework, right? So it's, you know, a good place to put things like how you know just patterns you know do's and don'ts as I've said so yeah let's get that done we can move any of the skills from uh if if a skill fits better like outside of the Claude skills directory um at least the knowledge base behind it so the skill itself could just be an on-demand you know it, we could leave the skill there so that the agents have this uh number one the skill description gives the overall awareness that this skill exists and two when the skill is then injected it just tells the model to read the readmes and and basically get, you know gives a quick over maybe a quick overview of uh, uh of how how it works so you know the skill could still exist however most of the knowledge of that skill should be in browsable form within these like system uh directories


